    "poster_id": 311437,
    "post_rendered": "Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\"  width=\"9\" height=\"8\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\"  width=\"8\" height=\"12\" > be two positive integers. Prove that the integer<br>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/5/14509b500811314c0c363da994e6de875ba468ba.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^2+\\left\\lceil\\frac{4a^2}b\\right\\rceil\\]\"  width=\"85\" height=\"43\" >is not a square. (Here <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/8/d2838937a3c11f25412016721df30396d9d7ce49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lceil z\\rceil$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"22\" height=\"19\" > denotes the least integer greater than or equal to <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\"  width=\"8\" height=\"8\" >.</span>)<br>\n<br>\n<i>Russia</i>",
    "post_canonical": "Let $a$ and $b$ be two positive integers. Prove that the integer\n\\[a^2+\\left\\lceil\\frac{4a^2}b\\right\\rceil\\]\nis not a square. (Here $\\lceil z\\rceil$ denotes the least integer greater than or equal to $z$.)\n\n[i]Russia[/i]",
